IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-rates`

-- Local Government Act 1995 (WA), Part 6 Division 6 (rates and service charges) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people
-- ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters, for the site's question form.
--
-- PURPOSE. One deployment serves every seat. Every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes
-- you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input, so the form
-- never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. (1) `I own land in a local government district`: the baseline's seat, the ratepayer, the owner for the time
-- being who is liable for the rates (s 6.44(1)). (2) `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns`: the lessee or
-- occupier, on whom the Act puts its own duties and liabilities: to pay rent to the local government on a s 6.60 notice,
-- to disclose the owner on request (s 6.61), and a service charge may be imposed on occupiers (s 6.38(1)(b)). The local
-- government, the Minister and the State Administrative Tribunal are never seats; what they may or must do appears as what
-- it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (as in the Graffiti Vandalism Act layer, design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else when it does not hold. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character.
-- The owner's situations: my land became rateable during the year (s 6.53); I became the owner part way through the
-- period (s 6.52); my local government imposes differential general rates (s 6.33(3)); my rates have been reassessed
-- (s 6.40(3)); I pay by instalments (ss 6.41(2)(b), 6.45, 6.50(3)); my unpaid rates (none overdue, some overdue, or the
-- land taken into possession: ss 6.51, 6.56, 6.64, 6.67, 6.69); my objection to the rate record (none, undecided,
-- decided: ss 6.77, 6.81). The tenant's or occupier's: a s 6.60 notice given to me (s 6.60(2)-(6)); a request from the
-- local government under s 6.61 (s 6.61(1), (2)).
--
-- The rules are in lga-rates.l4. For the owner this module calls them and restates none; each answer equals the
-- baseline export's wherever the role and situation hold. The tenant's questions use the baseline's rules where they
-- exist (ss 1.4 and 6.44(1), s 6.60(2), s 6.61) and small helpers below from the deposited text where they do not.
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- Conventions, as in the baseline: a day is the number YYYYMMDD; money in dollars; a rate in the dollar a decimal; an
-- interest rate a percentage a year.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Local Government Act 1995 (WA) -- rates: the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own land in a local government district`
    `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `a number of days` HAS `how many days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Interest rate` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `a rate of interest` HAS `percent a year` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Text answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the text` IS A STRING

-- The baseline's own answer types, each carried inside an answer that can also say `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Valuation answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `rated on` HAS `the basis of valuation` IS A `Valuation basis`

DECLARE `Which valuation answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `worked out on` HAS `the valuation used` IS A `Which valuation`

DECLARE `Overpayment answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `for the overpayment` HAS `what happens to it` IS A `What happens to an overpayment`

DECLARE `Paying answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `I may pay by` HAS `the ways to pay` IS A `How I may pay`

DECLARE `Stopping the sale answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `as to stopping the sale` HAS `what I can do` IS A `Can I stop the sale`

DECLARE `Complaint answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the complaint goes to` HAS `the route` IS A `Where my complaint goes`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `The situations a question arises in`

-- The owner's unpaid-rates situation. Interest (s 6.51), suing (s 6.56), possession (s 6.64(1)) and the caveat
-- (s 6.64(3)) arise once rates are unpaid after becoming due; giving the land back (s 6.67) and stopping a sale (s 6.69)
-- only once the local government has taken possession under s 6.64(1).
DECLARE `My unpaid rates` IS ONE OF
    `none of my rates is unpaid after its due date`
    `some of my rates are unpaid after their due date`
    `the local government has taken possession of my land for unpaid rates`

-- The owner's objection situation: review in the Tribunal (s 6.77) follows a decision on the objection; s 6.81 speaks
-- of liability "pending determination of the objection".
DECLARE `My objection` IS ONE OF
    `I have not objected to the rate record`
    `I have objected, and my objection has not yet been decided`
    `the local government has decided my objection`

-- These helpers list every value and have no OTHERWISE: on the stable l4 a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE quietly takes the
-- OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value (Graffiti Vandalism Act layer, finding 31), so a case could not show that an
-- ASSUMEd situation is never read; without OTHERWISE it fails if it is.
GIVEN `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `none of my rates is overdue` IF
    CONSIDER `my unpaid rates`
    WHEN `none of my rates is unpaid after its due date` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some of my rates are unpaid after their due date` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the local government has taken possession of my land for unpaid rates` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the local government has not taken possession of my land` IF
    CONSIDER `my unpaid rates`
    WHEN `none of my rates is unpaid after its due date` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some of my rates are unpaid after their due date` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the local government has taken possession of my land for unpaid rates` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `my objection` IS A `My objection`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my objection has not been decided` IF
    CONSIDER `my objection`
    WHEN `I have not objected to the rate record` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I have objected, and my objection has not yet been decided` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the local government has decided my objection` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `my objection` IS A `My objection`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no objection of mine is waiting to be decided` IF
    CONSIDER `my objection`
    WHEN `I have not objected to the rate record` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `I have objected, and my objection has not yet been decided` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the local government has decided my objection` THEN TRUE

§§ `For the owner of land (the ratepayer)`

§§§ `s 6.26, s 6.53 -- is my land rateable`

@export Is my land rateable land (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.26)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my land` IS A `What my land is` @desc What the land is and how it is used
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the land I own rateable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Is my land rateable` `my land`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export My land became rateable during the financial year: how much of the year's rates must I pay (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.53)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my land became rateable during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land became rateable land part way through the financial year (for example Crown land sold to you)
      `the rates for a full year` IS A NUMBER @desc The rates that would be payable for the whole financial year
      `days in the year the land is rateable` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of the financial year during which the land is rateable
      `days in the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc 365, or 366 in a leap year
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the year's rates must I pay now my land has become rateable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `my land became rateable during the financial year`
        THEN amount (`How much of the year's rates must I pay for land that became rateable` `the rates for a full year` `days in the year the land is rateable` `days in the financial year`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6.32, 6.43, 6.44, 6.52, 6.55 -- who levies the rates, and who must pay them`

@export Who levies rates on my land (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.32(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`Who levies the rates on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `the answer is` `Who levies rates on my home`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Am I liable to pay the rates on my land (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.44(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am the owner for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the owner of the land (s 1.4), for example the registered proprietor in possession
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I the person liable to pay the rates on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Am I liable to pay the rates` `I am the owner for the time being`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be made to pay all the rates on land I own with others (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.44(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `number of owners` IS A NUMBER @desc How many owners the land has, you included
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be made to pay all the rates on land I own jointly` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be made to pay all the rates on land I own with others` `number of owners`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Are unpaid rates a charge on my land (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are the rates a charge on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` `Are unpaid rates a charge on my land`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Can the rates on my land be recovered from me (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.55(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was the owner when the rate record was compiled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owned the land when the rate record for the year was compiled
      `I became the owner while the rates were unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became the owner while those rates were still unpaid
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the local government recover the rates on my land from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Can the rates be recovered from me` `I was the owner when the rate record was compiled` `I became the owner while the rates were unpaid`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, what share of the rates for the period is mine as between me and the seller (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.52(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I became the owner part way through the period the rates are for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought or otherwise became the owner of the land part way through the period (usually the financial year) for which the rates were imposed
      `the rates for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The rates imposed for the period (usually the financial year)
      `days in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc Days in the period for which the rates were imposed
      `days I own the land in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of that period from the day you became owner
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What share of the rates is mine as between me and the seller` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `I became the owner part way through the period the rates are for`
        THEN amount (`What share of the year's rates is mine as buyer` `the rates for the period` `days in the period` `days I own the land in the period`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export As a buyer, does sharing the rates with the seller change what the local government can recover from me (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.52(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I became the owner part way through the period the rates are for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought or otherwise became the owner of the land part way through the period (usually the financial year) for which the rates were imposed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does sharing the rates with the seller change what I can be made to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `I became the owner part way through the period the rates are for`
        THEN `yes if` `Does apportionment change what the council can recover from me`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 6.28 -- the valuation my rates are worked out on`

@export On what valuation is my land rated, gross rental value or unimproved value (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.28(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the determination` IS A `The Minister's determination for my land` @desc The method of valuation the Minister has determined for your land, if you know it
      `used predominantly for rural purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land is used predominantly for rural purposes
GIVETH A `Valuation answer`
`Is my land rated on gross rental value or unimproved value` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `rated on` (`On what valuation is my land rated` `the determination` `used predominantly for rural purposes`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Which valuation of my land are my rates worked out on this year (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.28(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an interim, amended or new valuation was made during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, during the financial year, an interim valuation, an amended valuation or a new valuation in a general valuation came into force for your land
GIVETH A `Which valuation answer`
`Which valuation are this year's rates worked out on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `worked out on` (`Which valuation are my rates worked out on` `an interim, amended or new valuation was made during the year`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6.32, 6.33, 6.35, 6.36 -- how much are my rates`

@export How much are my general rates, after any minimum payment (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) ss 6.32(2), 6.35(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the valuation` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross rental value or unimproved value of your land in the rate record, in dollars
      `the rate in the dollar` IS A NUMBER @desc The general rate (or your differential rate) as a decimal, for example 0.07 for 7 cents in the dollar
      `the minimum payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum payment the local government imposed for your rating category, or 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much are the general rates on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN amount (`How much are my general rates` `the valuation` `the rate in the dollar` `the minimum payment`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Am I paying the minimum payment rather than the rate in the dollar (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.35(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the valuation` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross rental value or unimproved value of your land in the rate record, in dollars
      `the rate in the dollar` IS A NUMBER @desc The general rate (or your differential rate) as a decimal, for example 0.07 for 7 cents in the dollar
      `the minimum payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum payment the local government imposed for your rating category, or 0 if none
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I paying the minimum payment rather than the rate in the dollar` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Am I paying the minimum payment` `the valuation` `the rate in the dollar` `the minimum payment`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export What is the total on my rate notice for rates and service charges (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.32(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the valuation` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross rental value or unimproved value of your land in the rate record, in dollars
      `the rate in the dollar` IS A NUMBER @desc The general rate (or your differential rate) as a decimal, for example 0.07 for 7 cents in the dollar
      `the minimum payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum payment the local government imposed for your rating category, or 0 if none
      `specified area rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Any specified area rate on your land, in dollars, or 0
      `service charges` IS A NUMBER @desc Any service charges on your land, in dollars, or 0
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the total of the rates and service charges on my notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN amount (`What is the total of my rates and service charges` `the valuation` `the rate in the dollar` `the minimum payment` `specified area rate` `service charges`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Is the differential general rate on my land within the limit of twice the lowest (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.33(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my local government imposes differential general rates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your local government imposes differential general rates (different rates for land of different zoning, use or vacancy)
      `my differential rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The differential general rate on your land, as a decimal
      `the lowest differential rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The lowest differential general rate the local government imposed
      `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister approved a higher rate
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the differential general rate on my land within the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `my local government imposes differential general rates`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my differential rate within the limit` `my differential rate` `the lowest differential rate` `the Minister approved`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export How many days do I have to make a submission on proposed differential rates or minimum payments (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.36(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period for submissions stated in the notice, in days, or 0 if none stated
GIVETH A `Days`
`How long do I have to make a submission on proposed rates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `a number of days` (`How many days do I have to make a submission` `days specified in the notice`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6.33(4), 6.39-6.41 -- my rate notice, and changes during the year`

@export Can my rate notice be sent to me by email (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.41(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I consented to email` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consented to receiving rate notices by email
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my rate notice be sent to me by email` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Can my rate notice be emailed` `I consented to email`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Is my rate notice served if it was delivered to the address in the rate record, even if I did not get it (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.41(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `delivered to the address in the rate record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was delivered to the address shown for you in the rate record
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my rate notice been served on me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Is my rate notice served` `delivered to the address in the rate record`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Must my rates for this year be reassessed (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) ss 6.33(4), 6.40(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the rateable value changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rateable value of your land changed during the year (for example an interim valuation after a house was built)
      `the rateability changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land became, or ceased to be, rateable
      `the rate imposed on it changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rate imposed on your land changed
      `only the land's differential rating characteristics changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only change was in the use, zoning or vacancy on which a differential rate is based
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the rates on my land be reassessed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Must my rates be reassessed` `the rateable value changed` `the rateability changed` `the rate imposed on it changed` `only the land's differential rating characteristics changed`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export My rates were reassessed: if I paid more than the reassessed rates, do I get a refund (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.40(3)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my rates for this year have been reassessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government has reassessed your rates for this year and given you notice of it (s 6.40(1))
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What you have paid for the year
      `the reassessed rates` IS A NUMBER @desc The rates for the year after reassessment
      `I asked for a refund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (the current owner) asked for a refund
GIVETH AN `Overpayment answer`
`If I have overpaid after the reassessment, do I get a refund` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `my rates for this year have been reassessed`
        THEN `for the overpayment` (`Do I get a refund of overpaid rates` `the amount paid` `the reassessed rates` `I asked for a refund`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6.45, 6.46, 6.50 -- when my rates are due, and paying by instalments`

@export What is the fewest days after my rate notice was issued that my rates can fall due (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.50(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Days`
`How soon after my rate notice was issued can my rates fall due` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `a number of days` `What is the fewest days after the notice that my rates can fall due`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Is the due date on my rate notice lawful (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.50(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the issue date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date the notice says it was issued, as YYYYMMDD
      `the due date` IS A NUMBER @desc The due date on the notice (or of the first instalment), as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the due date on my rate notice lawful` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Is my due date lawful` `the issue date` `the due date`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

-- Asked of every owner; the reassessment is an ordinary input here (the same input as the s 6.40(3) situation), since an
-- owner whose rates were not reassessed still asks how they may pay.
@export How may I pay my rates (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.45(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my rates for this year have been reassessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government has reassessed your rates for this year and given you notice of it (s 6.40(1))
GIVETH A `Paying answer`
`How may I pay the rates on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `I may pay by` (`How may I pay my rates` `my rates for this year have been reassessed`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export I pay by instalments: how much is each of my 4 instalments, with any instalment charge (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.45(1)(a), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I pay my rates by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have chosen to pay your rates by instalments rather than in one payment (s 6.45(1))
      `the rates and service charges` IS A NUMBER @desc The total on your rate notice
      `the instalment charge` IS A NUMBER @desc The additional charge the local government imposes for paying by instalments, in total
      `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a rebate or deferment under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (or one the local government resolved to give)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much is each of my 4 instalments` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `I pay my rates by instalments`
        THEN amount (`How much is each instalment` `the rates and service charges` `the instalment charge` `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export I pay by instalments: is this instalment's due date lawful (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.50(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I pay my rates by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have chosen to pay your rates by instalments rather than in one payment (s 6.45(1))
      `the previous instalment's due date` IS A NUMBER @desc The due date of the previous instalment, as YYYYMMDD
      `this instalment's due date` IS A NUMBER @desc The due date of this instalment, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the due date of this instalment lawful` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `I pay my rates by instalments`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is this instalment due date lawful` `the previous instalment's due date` `this instalment's due date`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export I pay by instalments: was I given my instalment notice early enough (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.41(2)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I pay my rates by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have chosen to pay your rates by instalments rather than in one payment (s 6.45(1))
      `the day the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the instalment notice was given to you, as YYYYMMDD
      `the instalment's due date` IS A NUMBER @desc The due date of the instalment, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was my instalment notice given to me early enough` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `I pay my rates by instalments`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was my instalment notice early enough` `the day the notice was given` `the instalment's due date`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Do I get a discount for paying my rates early (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the local government resolved a discount when imposing the rates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the council resolved, when imposing the rates, to give a discount or incentive for early payment
      `I paid by the discount date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid in time to meet the terms of that discount
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I get a discount for paying my rates early` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Do I get an early payment discount` `the local government resolved a discount when imposing the rates` `I paid by the discount date`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 6.51 -- interest on late rates, and the rebates connection`

-- In the situation the rates are unpaid after the due date, so the baseline's own input of that fact is TRUE by the
-- situation's terms and is not asked again.
@export Some of my rates are overdue: does interest run on them (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.51(1), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
      `the local government resolved to charge interest when imposing the rates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the council resolved, when imposing the rates, to charge interest on overdue amounts
      `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a rebate or deferment under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (or one the local government resolved to give)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does interest run on the rates I have not paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `none of my rates is overdue` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does interest run on my overdue rates` `the local government resolved to charge interest when imposing the rates` TRUE `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Some of my rates are overdue: what is the highest rate of interest I can be charged on them, % a year (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.51(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
      `the rate in the budget` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest rate set in the local government's annual budget, % a year
      `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum rate prescribed by regulations, % a year
GIVETH AN `Interest rate`
`What is the highest rate of interest I can be charged on my overdue rates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `none of my rates is overdue` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `a rate of interest` (`What is the highest interest rate I can be charged` `the rate in the budget` `the prescribed maximum`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Some of my rates are overdue: about how much interest will I be charged (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.51, simple daily interest assumed)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
      `the amount overdue` IS A NUMBER @desc The rates or instalment unpaid after the due date, in dollars
      `the rate in the budget` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest rate set in the local government's annual budget, % a year
      `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum rate prescribed by regulations, % a year
      `the due date` IS A NUMBER @desc The due date on the notice (or of the first instalment), as YYYYMMDD
      `the day I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you pay, as YYYYMMDD
      `the local government resolved to charge interest when imposing the rates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the council resolved, when imposing the rates, to charge interest on overdue amounts
      `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a rebate or deferment under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (or one the local government resolved to give)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`About how much interest will I be charged on my overdue rates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `none of my rates is overdue` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`About how much interest will I be charged` `the amount overdue` `the rate in the budget` `the prescribed maximum` `the due date` `the day I pay` `the local government resolved to charge interest when imposing the rates` `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Where do I find the pensioner and seniors rebates and deferments of rates?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`Where do I find the pensioner and seniors rebates and deferments` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `the answer is` `Where are the pensioner and seniors rebates and deferments`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Subdivision 5 -- recovery of unpaid rates`

@export Some of my rates are overdue: can the local government sue me for them (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.56(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the local government sue me for my unpaid rates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `none of my rates is overdue` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the local government sue me for my rates` TRUE)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Is my payment applied to my oldest rates first (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.62)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my payment applied to the oldest rates first` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` `Is my payment applied to my oldest rates first`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Subdivision 6 -- what can be done to my land if rates stay unpaid`

@export Some of my rates are overdue: can the local government take possession of my land for them (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.64(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
      `years the oldest unpaid rates have been unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc How long the oldest unpaid rates have been unpaid, in years
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the local government take possession of my land for my unpaid rates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `none of my rates is overdue` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the local government take possession of my land` `years the oldest unpaid rates have been unpaid`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Some of my rates are overdue: can the local government lodge a caveat over my land for them (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.64(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the local government lodge a caveat over my land for my unpaid rates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `none of my rates is overdue` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the local government lodge a caveat over my land` TRUE)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export The local government has taken possession of my land: if I pay all the arrears, must it give my land back (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.67(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
      `years since possession was taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How long ago the local government took possession, in years
      `the land has been sold or transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has already sold the land or transferred it to the Crown or itself
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If I pay all the arrears, must the local government give my land back to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `the local government has not taken possession of my land` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the local government give my land back` `years since possession was taken` `the land has been sold or transferred`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export The local government has taken possession of my land: can I stop its sale by paying the arrears (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.69)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my unpaid rates` IS A `My unpaid rates` @desc Whether any of your rates or service charges (or an instalment) is unpaid after its due date, and whether the local government has taken possession of your land for rates unpaid for at least 3 years (s 6.64)
      `days before the sale` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the time of the sale you would pay (0 or less if the sale has happened)
GIVETH A `Stopping the sale answer`
`Can I stop the sale of my land by paying the arrears` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `the local government has not taken possession of my land` `my unpaid rates`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `as to stopping the sale` (`Can I stop the sale by paying` `days before the sale`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Subdivision 7 -- objecting to my rates`

-- Asked of every owner; whether the local government imposes differential general rates is an ordinary input here,
-- read only for a complaint about the rating category (the same input as the s 6.33(3) situation).
@export Where does my complaint about my rates go (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) ss 6.76, 6.80, 6.82)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my complaint` IS A `My complaint` @desc What you say is wrong
      `my local government imposes differential general rates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your local government imposes differential general rates (different rates for land of different zoning, use or vacancy)
GIVETH A `Complaint answer`
`Where does my complaint about my rates go to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `the complaint goes to` (`Where does my complaint go` `my complaint` `my local government imposes differential general rates`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export Is my objection to the rate record validly made (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.76(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days since the rate notice was served` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from service of the rate notice to the day you lodge the objection
      `the local government extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government extended the time for you
      `in writing, identifying the land, with full and detailed grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the objection is in writing, identifies the land and sets out the grounds fully and in detail
      `I am the owner named in the rate record, or their agent or attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the owner named in the rate record, or that owner's agent or attorney
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my objection to the rate record validly made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `yes if` (`Is my objection validly made` `days since the rate notice was served` `the local government extended the time` `in writing, identifying the land, with full and detailed grounds` `I am the owner named in the rate record, or their agent or attorney`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export My objection has been decided: am I in time to ask the State Administrative Tribunal to review the decision (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.77)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my objection to the rate record` IS A `My objection` @desc Whether you have objected to the rate record under s 6.76, and if so whether the local government has decided your objection
      `days since notice of the decision was served` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from service of the notice of the decision on your objection
      `the Tribunal allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Administrative Tribunal allowed you more time for reasonable cause
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in time to ask the State Administrative Tribunal for a review` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `my objection has not been decided` `my objection to the rate record`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I in time to apply for a review` `days since notice of the decision was served` `the Tribunal allowed a further period`)
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

@export My objection is waiting to be decided: must I still pay my rates meanwhile (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.81)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my objection to the rate record` IS A `My objection` @desc Whether you have objected to the rate record under s 6.76, and if so whether the local government has decided your objection
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I keep paying my rates while my objection is decided` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN
        IF `no objection of mine is waiting to be decided` `my objection to the rate record`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `Must I still pay while my objection is decided`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the tenant or occupier of land someone else owns`

-- The baseline asked two of these from the owner's seat (s 6.60(2) "As a tenant, must I pay my rent to the local
-- government", and the s 6.61 fine); here they belong to the tenant's role, and call the same baseline functions.

-- Helpers from the deposited text where the baseline has no rule.
--
-- s 6.38(1): "A local government may impose on -- (a) owners; or (b) occupiers, of land within the district or a defined
-- part of the district a service charge for a financial year to meet the cost to the local government in the provision
-- of a prescribed work, service or facility in relation to the land."
`s 6.38(1)(b) -- a service charge may be imposed on occupiers` MEANS TRUE

-- s 6.60(4): "The local government may recover the amount of the rate or service charge as a debt from the lessee if
-- rent is not paid in accordance with the notice."
GIVEN `I paid my rent to the local government as the notice requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6.60(4) -- the rates may be recovered from the lessee as a debt` IF
    NOT `I paid my rent to the local government as the notice requires`

-- s 6.60(5): "Where an amount is paid under this section to the local government -- (a) the payment discharges the payer
-- from any liability to any person to pay that amount as rent; and (b) where as between a lessor and lessee the lessor is
-- liable to pay the rate or service charge, the amount paid may be set off by the lessee against the rent payable to the
-- lessor; and (c) if the amount exceeds the rent due, or if there is no rent due, the amount may be set off by the lessee
-- against accruing rent, or the balance recovered from the lessor in a court of competent jurisdiction."
-- (6): "To the extent that an agreement purports to preclude a lessee from setting off or recovering payments made to a
-- local government under this section, the agreement is of no effect."
`s 6.60(5)(a) -- the payment discharges the lessee from paying that amount as rent` MEANS TRUE

GIVEN `as between me and my landlord, my landlord is liable for the rates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6.60(5)(b) -- the lessee may set off the payment against the rent` IF
    `as between me and my landlord, my landlord is liable for the rates`

`s 6.60(5)(c) -- an excess may be set off against accruing rent or recovered from the lessor` MEANS TRUE

`s 6.60(6) -- an agreement cannot preclude the set off or recovery` MEANS TRUE

-- s 6.61(1): "On the request of a local government -- (a) the occupier of property, or an agent of the owner of
-- property, is required to disclose to the local government the name and address of the owner or of the person receiving
-- or authorised to receive the rent of the property".
`s 6.61(1)(a) -- the occupier must disclose the owner on request` MEANS TRUE

§§§ `ss 1.4, 6.38, 6.44 -- what I may be charged`

-- s 1.4, "owner" (a)(ii): "a Crown lessee or a lessee or tenant under a lease or tenancy agreement of the land which in
-- the hands of the lessor is not rateable land under this Act, but which in the hands of the lessee or tenant is by reason
-- of the lease or tenancy rateable land". Such a tenant is the owner, and liable under s 6.44(1); any other tenant is not.
@export Am I liable to pay the rates on the land I rent (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) ss 1.4 "owner", 6.44(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the land is rateable only because of my lease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is not rateable in your landlord's hands (for example Crown land) but is rateable in yours because of your lease or tenancy
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I liable to pay the rates on the land I rent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `yes if` (`Am I liable to pay the rates` `the land is rateable only because of my lease`)

@export Can the local government charge me a service charge as the occupier of the land (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.38(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be charged a service charge as the occupier` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN `yes if` `s 6.38(1)(b) -- a service charge may be imposed on occupiers`

§§§ `s 6.60 -- a notice to pay my rent to the local government`

-- In the notice situation the baseline's own input "I was given a notice under s 6.60" is TRUE by the situation's terms
-- and is not asked again.
@export I was given a notice under s 6.60: must I pay my rent to the local government instead of my landlord (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.60(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government gave you a notice under s 6.60 requiring you to pay your rent to it, as it falls due, towards the rates on the land
      `the landlord's rates are due and payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether rates on the land you lease are due and unpaid
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pay my rent to the local government instead of my landlord` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I pay my rent to the local government` `the landlord's rates are due and payable` TRUE)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

@export I was given a notice under s 6.60: if I do not pay my rent to the local government as it requires, can the local government recover the rates from me as a debt (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.60(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government gave you a notice under s 6.60 requiring you to pay your rent to it, as it falls due, towards the rates on the land
      `I paid my rent to the local government as the notice requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid your rent, as it fell due, to the local government as the notice requires
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If I do not pay my rent to the local government as the notice requires, can it recover the rates from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government`
        THEN `yes if` (`s 6.60(4) -- the rates may be recovered from the lessee as a debt` `I paid my rent to the local government as the notice requires`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

@export I was given a notice under s 6.60: does what I pay the local government count as rent paid, so that my landlord cannot ask me for it again (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.60(5)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government gave you a notice under s 6.60 requiring you to pay your rent to it, as it falls due, towards the rates on the land
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does paying my rent to the local government count as paying it to my landlord` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government`
        THEN `yes if` `s 6.60(5)(a) -- the payment discharges the lessee from paying that amount as rent`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

@export I was given a notice under s 6.60: can I set off what I paid the local government against the rent I owe my landlord (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.60(5)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government gave you a notice under s 6.60 requiring you to pay your rent to it, as it falls due, towards the rates on the land
      `as between me and my landlord, my landlord is liable for the rates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as between you and your landlord (under your lease), it is the landlord who must pay the rates or service charge
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I set off what I paid the local government against the rent I owe my landlord` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government`
        THEN `yes if` (`s 6.60(5)(b) -- the lessee may set off the payment against the rent` `as between me and my landlord, my landlord is liable for the rates`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

@export I was given a notice under s 6.60: if I paid the local government more than the rent then due, or when no rent was due, can I set it off against later rent or recover the balance from my landlord (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.60(5)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government gave you a notice under s 6.60 requiring you to pay your rent to it, as it falls due, towards the rates on the land
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If I paid the local government more than the rent then due, can I get the balance back` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government`
        THEN `yes if` `s 6.60(5)(c) -- an excess may be set off against accruing rent or recovered from the lessor`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

-- The answer is no whatever the lease says: s 6.60(6) makes such a term of no effect.
@export I was given a notice under s 6.60: can a term of my lease stop me setting off or recovering what I paid the local government (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.60(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government gave you a notice under s 6.60 requiring you to pay your rent to it, as it falls due, towards the rates on the land
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my lease stop me setting off or recovering what I paid the local government` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `I was given a notice to pay my rent to the local government`
        THEN `yes if` (NOT `s 6.60(6) -- an agreement cannot preclude the set off or recovery`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 6.61 -- telling the local government who owns the property`

@export The local government has asked me: must I tell it the name and address of the owner, or of the person who receives the rent (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.61(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the local government has asked me who owns the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government has asked you, as occupier, for the name and address of the owner of the property or of the person who receives or may receive its rent
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I tell the local government who owns the property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `the local government has asked me who owns the property`
        THEN `yes if` `s 6.61(1)(a) -- the occupier must disclose the owner on request`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

@export The local government has asked me: what is the most I can be fined for not telling it who owns the property, or for giving false or misleading information (Local Government Act 1995 (WA) s 6.61(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the local government has asked me who owns the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government has asked you, as occupier, for the name and address of the owner of the property or of the person who receives or may receive its rent
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not telling the local government who owns the property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land in a local government district` THEN `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I rent or occupy land that someone else owns` THEN
        IF `the local government has asked me who owns the property`
        THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined for not naming the owner`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
